From 11391ba54c52971f40dd6d858dd046393c390d9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kasniya <36neelansh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:23:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(decorate): fewer reads and no state copies in lush cave
 patches

- vegetation_patch column walk: each position is read once (the outward
  walk's first step reuses the air the inward walk left, `below` reuses
  the last solid read for the sturdy face and the first ground step), and
  a ground step that finds the ground's own block returns at once instead
  of re-asking the same question `depth` times. PosSet no longer hashes:
  every patch inserts positions of distinct columns.
- StateProvider::state_ref: the same draws as `state`, handing back the
  configured state by reference; randomized_int providers over a
  Simple/Weighted source precompute every rolled state (with its
  `knows` answer) at compile time.
- simple_block and block_column write configured states by reference
  (set_block_ref) instead of cloning; the two-block plant writes its lower
  half by reference unless its waterlogging changes.
- block_column: a local, quiet allowed_placement predicate is answered
  once per state key per call.
- Survival rule tags use AHashSet (lookups only).

Random draws, write order, written states and state interning order are
unchanged; pregen digest df701ee858e2bdd3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
